if the UN hadn't already made severe  cuts to its budget it wouldn't have had  enough money to stage the high-level  week of the UN General Assembly when  world leaders visited New York last  month  Secretary General Antonio Guterres said  the organization is confronting its  worst financial situation in a decade  the organization is facing a severe  financial crisis to be more specific as  severe liquidity crisis the equation is  simple without cash the budget cannot be  properly implemented our work and our  reforms are at risk the  secretary-general was very clear about  the dire problems the UN is facing but  at no point did he list the countries  that are causing it by not paying what  they owe and surely you've got a big  problem here and you need to name the  people responsible for it there's 193  member states 129 have paid up in full  the balance that's not of those who  haven't paid the US which has the  largest GDP in the world owes by far the  most a sum of over 1 billion and 55  million dollars that's more than all the  other 63 countries on the list of those  who haven't paid put together the u.s.  also owes well over 2 billion dollars to  the separate UN peacekeeping budget  James BAE's al Jazeera of the United  Nations
 

